\[B = (\sin 60^\circ \cos 45^\circ, \sin 60^\circ \sin 45^\circ, \cos 60^\circ) = \left( \frac{\sqrt{6}}{4}, \frac{\sqrt{6}}{4}, \frac{1}{2} \right).\]Then the shortest path from $A$ to $B$ along the surface of the Earth is arc $AB,$ where the center of the arc is the center of the Earth $O.$  By symmetry, the northernmost point on this arc is the midpoint of the arc.  Let this midpoint be $C,$ so $C$ lies in the $xz$-plane.

